|title=<span>Fun Facts</span>
|body=<includeonly>{{Choose
| [[File:Ambush sprite.png|200px|center|link=Ambush|class=notpageimage|Ambush]]
[[Ambush]] is a very persistent [[List of Entities|entity]], unlike [[Rush]], if it encounters a room with a blocked/locked door it will phase through the door, nothing can stop the power of Ambush tripping up the [[player]], take care.
| [[File:Timothy render.png|200px|center|link=Timothy|class=notpageimage|Timothy]]
[[Timothy]] is one of the smallest [[List of Entities|entities]] in ''[[DOORS]]'', due to its size it is smaller than every furniture item within the game, which allows it to hide in [[containers]] among [[Gold]] and [[items]].
| [[File:DOORS Icon.png|200px|center|link=DOORS|class=notpageimage|DOORS]]
During the initial release of ''[[DOORS]]'' the game played an animation for [[Player|players]] crawling under furniture during [[Seek]]'s chase sequences, this was removed due to players with bad latency and terrible internet dying due to the animation failing to load or loading too late.
| [[File:Jacky.webp|200px|center|link=Jack|class=notpageimage|Jack]]
[[Jack]] can not only appear in the [[Hiding|closets]] scattered across various rooms in [[The Hotel]], it is also known to make an appearance behind recently opened doors. When this occurs, the room will receive a blood-red tone. This effect also applies to the rain if it is present outside.
| [[File:Old Seek.png|200px|center|link=Seek|class=notpageimage]]
[[Seek]] was the first [[List of Entities|entity]], being added in-game before the rest. It also had a very different design than what it is now, appearing much more limp and having a different facial structure.
| [[File:Eyeopt2.webp|200px|center|link=Eyes|class=notpageimage]]
The [[Eyes]] are known to be able to spawn in certain rooms that none of the other [[List of Entities|entities]] can. Such rooms can include [[The Courtyard]] and [[The Dining Room]]. However, that is not to say that entities are physically limited from The Courtyard, as [[Rush]] and [[Ambush]] can pass through if they happen to be activated in the succeeding area.
| [[File:Screech render.png|200px|center|link=Screech|class=notpageimage]]
The 'Psst!' sound [[Screech]] vocalizes does not indicate its appearance in the room, but rather when it will attack a [[player]]. Also, some instances of this sound may be falsified, being played solely to startle the player. Pay attention to the volume, as the fake one is quieter.
| [[File:OldyFiguor.png|200px|center|link=Figure|class=notpageimage]]
This was one of [[Figure]]'s earliest models, during the game's early development stages. Yes, the design has changed a lot! Another fact about Figure is that the name 'Figure' was actually the placeholder name for this entity during the game's development. Before release, the developers actually liked the name 'Figure', so they made it official.
| [[File:GLITCH11.png|200px|center|link=Glitch|class=notpageimage]]
[[Glitch]] is a canon [[List of Entities|entity]], meaning it has a role in the lore. During the initial release, it solely appeared to prey on stray wanderers that were too far from their group ahead. However, it currently exists as a failsafe for faulty room generation with the previously mentioned mechanic being given to [[Void]].
| [[File:El Goblino render.png|200px|center|link=El Goblino|class=notpageimage]]
[[El Goblino]] is the [[List of Entities|entity]] responsible for generating various ambient noises by thumping on walls and doors in [[The Hotel]]. It does this in order to scare humans for its own amusement, though it does not mean any harm as seen with its amiable behavior.
| [[File:The_Rooms_Fixed.PNG|200px|center|link=The Rooms|class=notpageimage]]
Before it was replaced by [[The Archives]], [[The Rooms]] was a modified [[Floors|floor]] that originated from one of the games that inspired ''[[DOORS]]''' creation, simply known as [https://r-rooms.fandom.com/wiki/Roblox_ROOMS_Wiki Rooms]. Its existence in ''DOORS'' was an official collaboration with its creator, [https://r-rooms.fandom.com/wiki/Nicorocks5555 nicorocks5555].
| [[File:Snareoutline3.png|200px|center|link=Snare|class=notpageimage]]
[[Snare]] is one of the only [[List of Entities|entities]] that is capable of harming [[Player|players]], but isn't capable of killing them on its own. The only other entities that does this is [[Timothy]] and [[Sally]].
| [[File:GreedNDepth.png|200px|center|link=Greed|class=notpageimage]]
The ''[[DOORS]]'' community has made countless fanmade [[List of Entities|entities]], although only two have made a complete appearance in-game. These entities would be [[Greed]], which only appears in the [[2023 April Fools Event|SUPER HARD MODE!!]] as an entity that attacks [[Player|players]] who loot [[Gold]] too often, and [[2023 April Fools Event#Rush Clones|Depth]] who is just a reskin of [[Rush]].
| [[File:Crucifix_&_Skeleton_Key_Icons.png|200px|center|link=Items|class=notpageimage]]
The [[Crucifix]] and [[Skeleton Key]] were both initially intended to be added in ''[[DOORS]]''' initial release, but were scrapped for unknown reasons. They were reimplemented in [[The Hotel+ Update]] as rare, but incredibly useful [[items]].
| [[File:Green Herb icon.png|200px|center|link=Green_Herb|class=notpageimage]]
The [[Green Herb]] is the first object in the game to give [[Player|players]] a passive [[Status Effects|effect]] upon interacting with it. Previously, interacting with it and entering a sub-floor (at the time only [[The Rooms]]) would remove this effect, but it has since been patched.
| [[File:Bob hotel render.png|200px|center|link=Bob|class=notpageimage]]
It is heavily implied that [[Bob]] isn't alive, and is just a pile of bones. [[El Goblino]] has mentioned that Bob got in a fight with [[Rush]] after accidentally stepping on [[Snare]], which is implied to have lead to his death. El Goblino also implies that Bob has recently died of starvation, mentioning that he looks like a "...real bag of bones."
| [[File:Void render.png|200px|center|link=Void|class=notpageimage]]
When [[The Hotel+ Update]] released, [[Void]] was used to replace [[Glitch]]'s function to teleport [[Player|players]] ahead when they were left behind in an unloading room and Glitch was changed to only be a failsafe, but in [[Floors#Subfloors|subfloors]] Glitch still carries its old function due to Void being absent.
| [[File:Moonlight render.png|200px|center|link=Guiding Light|class=notpageimage]]
[[Moonlight]] is present throughout the majority of ''[[DOORS]]'', assisting the [[player]] in several different ways, however, in [[The Archives]], [[The Backdoor]], [[The Outdoors]] and the [[The Stairwell]], Moonlight is completely absent and its related [[items]] don't function, supposedly feeling "lighter" than usual when held. [[Starlight]] takes Moonlight's place in these subfloors, and is much less reliable than her.
| [[File:CuriousLightRender3.png|200px|center|link=The Rooms|class=notpageimage]] [[File:The Rooms.mp3|200px|center]]
While it was still available, entering [[The Rooms]] would play a special sound effect that sounds like wind blowing. This is a reference to [https://r-rooms.fandom.com/wiki/Roblox_ROOMS_Wiki nicorocks' Rooms], in which [https://r-rooms.fandom.com/wiki/A-200 A-200's] despawn sound effect plays upon joining the game, which is a much louder sound of wind blowing.
| [[File:A-60 sprite.png|200px|center|link=A-60|class=notpageimage]]
[[A-60]] was the first [[List of Entities|entity]] in ''[[DOORS]]'' to make an appearance before officially being implemented into the game, as during one of [https://www.youtube.com/c/KreekCraft KreekCraft's] streams before the [[Update Logs|Hotel+ Update]] released a variant of [[A-60]] was activated as a troll entity to mess with Kreek.
| [[File:RushNSnareNew.png|200px|center|link=List_of_Entities|class=notpageimage]]
Sometimes, if a player is temporarily caught in a [[Snare]] trap in [[The Greenhouse]], there is a chance that [[Rush]] can also be coming through the room at the same time, this ends up becoming a combo kill against the player. These two [[List of Entities|entities]] do not work together to achieve this outcome, it is simply a coincidence. Be sure to take extra care the next time you're in [[The Greenhouse]] to avoid this deadly combo when it arises.
| [[File:Dread sprite.png|200px|center|link=Dread|class=notpageimage]]
[[Dread]] was previously a secret [[List of Entities|entity]] that could be encountered after one real-life hour had passed (at midnight in-game). Secondly, Door 13 had to be opened, whilst Door 14 remained unopened. When these requirements were met Dread would spawn, behaving as it does currently.
| [[File:Lookman sprite.png|200px|center|link=The_Backdoor#The_Lookman|class=notpageimage]]
[[The_Backdoor#The_Lookman|The Lookman]] is similar to [[Eyes]] in several ways, as not only does it hurt you when looked at, but its name is the previous name of Eyes, along with aspects of its design, such as its glowing eyes, resembling Eyes' old design!
| [[File:Haste1.png|200px|center|link=The Backdoor#Haste|class=notpageimage]]
[[The_Backdoor#Haste|Haste]] is a direct reference to [https://spookys-jump-scare-mansion.fandom.com/wiki/Specimen_9 Specimen 9] from [https://spookys-jump-scare-mansion.fandom.com/wiki/Spooky%27s_Jump_Scare_Mansion_Wiki Spooky's Jumpscare Mansion], both having similar appearances and death screens with repeating mantras, Haste's being "NO TIME LEFT" and Specimen 9's being "TO TAKE THE DEAD".
| [[File:ShearsIcon.webp|200px|center|link=Shears|class=notpageimage]]
The [[Shears]]' original function was cutting vine-covered [[Containers|chests]] in [[The Greenhouse]], but it felt like another [[Lockpick]], and it was unusual for an [[Items|item]] to only be useful in about 10 rooms in the entire [[Floors|floor]], so the item was shelved for future use. This idea was reimplemented into [[The Mines]], with vines reappearing throughout the floor.
| [[File:hasol.webp|200px|center|link=The Backdoor#Haste|class=notpageimage]] [[The Backdoor#Haste|Haste]] was originally planned to be in [[The Hotel]] rather than The Backdoor. Originally, if a [[player]] stalled in a room for too long, Haste would chase down the player and force them to [[Hiding|hide]]. The developers didn't like this mechanic, so Haste was scrapped and would be re-introduced with a new and better mechanic the following year.
| [[File:Eyemodifier.png|200px|center|link=Modifiers#Scrapped|class=notpageimage]] 
[[Eyes]] have multiple [[modifiers]] to their name, but one was scrapped. This modifier was called "Sightseeing", and it simply gave Eyes the ability to teleport, providing more of a challenge. This modifier was scrapped, and Eyes' ability to teleport was added to its [[The Mines|Mines]] upgrade, as well as its equivelant modifier for [[The Hotel]].
| [[File:NewQueenGrumbleRender.webp|200px|center|link=Queen Grumble|class=notpageimage]] 
Unlike normal [[Grumbles]], the [[Queen Grumble]] has extra buffs. Her movement speed is faster than any other Grumble, making her difficult to outrun. The [[Bulklight]] can still blind her, but she can still catch up to [[Player|players]] easily. She doesn't laugh, making it harder for players to sense if she is coming. She is slightly paler and larger than the other Grumbles, and features a large scar on her forehead. She first appears at the end of the first [[Seek]] chase in [[The Mines]], and chases you once the bridge has been powered.
| [[File:Gloombat render.png|200px|link=Gloombats|center|class=notpageimage]] 
[[Gloombats]] have eggs, and when stepped on, they will get hurt and more Gloombats will spawn. If a [[player]] dies by the Gloombats, they will lay eggs on the corpse.
| [[File:ScreechPileRender2.png|200px|link=Screech|center|class=notpageimage]]
It's heavily implied there are multiple [[Screech|Screeches]]. There are multiple dead Screech piles found in [[The Nest]], and [[El Goblino]] states that he's seen more than one Screech.
| [[File:Seek render.png|200px|center|link=The Rooms|center|class=notpageimage]]
Most entities were named by the player, rather then having their own names. Though, this does not include [[Moonlight]] and [[Starlight]], subfloor entities, the [[Jeff Shop]] trio entities, and [[Timothy]]. This may or may not include Louie or Sally.
| [[File:RushImgSpr.png|200px|center|link=List of Entities|center|class=notpageimage]]
[[Player|Players]] are able to obtain the [[Achievements|"In Plain Sight"]] badge through [[Rush]] and [[Ambush]]. However, they aren't able to obtain it through other Rush-like counterparts, like [[The Backdoor#Blitz|Blitz]], [[Surge]], [[Bash]], [[Scribbles]], [[AR0xMBUSH]], [[RNIUSHCg==]] and [[Drone|Drones Stampedes]]. This is likely an oversight by the [[:Category:Developers|developers]].
| [[File:A-120 sprite.png|200px|center|link=The Rooms|center|class=notpageimage]]
Before its removal, [[A-120]] would sometimes rebound. This made it the second entity to (intentionally) rebound, with the first being [[Ambush]].
| [[File:SuperHardModeIcon.png|200px|center|link=2023 April Fools Event|center|class=notpageimage]]
In [[2023 April Fools Event|SUPER HARD MODE!!!]], players needed to collect 15 books in [[The Library]]. This caused [[Figure]] to move much faster than usual. Figure could also have been killed by a [[Holy Hand Grenade]], which would produce this sound:<br>[[File:FigDeath in-game fixed.mp3]]<small>(Warning: LOUD)</small>
| [[File:Visions text2.png|200px|center|link=Visions|center|class=notpageimage]]
Before getting their '''official name''', Visions used to be listed in a floor category called "EVENT". This was however changed to be "Visions" as of the [[Cringle's Workshop Event|Cringle's Workshop]] Event.</small>
| [[File:Shadowoutlined.png|200px|center|link=Shadow|center|class=notpageimage]]
[[Weirdo]] is the most unknown [[List of Entities|entity]] in [[DOORS]]. Unlike other entities, it cannot be spawned through the [[Admin Panel|admin panel]] and doesn't have any death message from both [[The Three Architects|architects]]. The only information known about it is its appearance and that it jumpscares the player whenever it appears.</small>
| [[File:The Archives Update Icon.png|200px|center|link=The Archives Update|center|class=notpageimage]]
The [[The Archives Update|Archives update]] was the first [[Update Logs|update]] to remove a [[Floors|subfloor]]. Additionally, it was also the first one to add two subfloors.
